CAT = "cpabarDerivatives"; SEG = "DER"
Q = [
("Which feature is part of the definition of a derivative under ASC 815?",
 "Net settlement is permitted", ["It trades on an exchange", "It is held only to hedge", "It matures within a year"],
 "A derivative has an underlying and a notional amount or payment provision, little or no initial net investment, and terms that permit or require net settlement."),
("In a qualifying fair value hedge, the change in the fair value of the hedging derivative is recognized in:",
 "Earnings, with the hedged item", ["Other comprehensive income", "Retained earnings directly", "A deferred hedge asset"],
 "Both the derivative and the hedged asset or liability are marked to fair value for the hedged risk through earnings, so the changes offset in the same line."),
("In a qualifying cash flow hedge, the gain or loss on the hedging derivative is first recognized in:",
 "Other comprehensive income", ["Earnings when it arises", "The hedged item's balance", "Retained earnings directly"],
 "Cash flow hedge gains and losses go to other comprehensive income and are reclassified into earnings when the hedged transaction affects earnings."),
("A company holds a derivative that is not designated in a hedging relationship. Changes in its fair value are recognized in:",
 "Earnings as they occur", ["Other comprehensive income", "A deferred account", "Equity when settled"],
 "Derivatives are carried at fair value, and without hedge designation every change in fair value goes straight to earnings."),
("An embedded derivative is separated from its host contract when its economic features are not clearly and closely related to the host and:",
 "It would be a derivative alone", ["It is under a year to maturity", "The host is a lease", "The host is measured at cost"],
 "Bifurcation also requires that the hybrid contract is not carried at fair value through earnings and that a separate instrument with the same terms would meet the derivative definition."),
("To qualify for hedge accounting, the hedging relationship and risk management objective must be documented:",
 "At inception of the hedge", ["When it first proves effective", "At each fiscal year end", "When the hedge is settled"],
 "ASC 815 requires formal documentation at inception, including the hedged item, the hedging instrument, the risk hedged and how effectiveness will be assessed."),
("A company with fixed-rate debt enters a swap to receive fixed and pay variable, hedging changes in the debt's fair value from interest rates. The hedge is a:",
 "Fair value hedge", ["Cash flow hedge", "Net investment hedge", "Speculative position"],
 "Swapping fixed-rate debt to variable protects against changes in the debt's fair value, which makes it a fair value hedge."),
("A company with variable-rate debt enters a swap to pay fixed and receive variable, so its interest payments are fixed. The hedge is a:",
 "Cash flow hedge", ["Fair value hedge", "Net investment hedge", "Trading position"],
 "Fixing variable interest payments hedges the variability of future cash flows, which makes it a cash flow hedge."),
("A company pays fixed 4.0% and receives variable 4.6% on a $10,000,000 notional interest rate swap, settled annually. For the year, the net settlement is that the company:",
 "Receives $60,000", ["Pays $60,000", "Receives $460,000", "Pays $400,000"],
 "Only the difference is exchanged: (4.6% - 4.0%) x $10,000,000 = $60,000, received because the variable rate it receives is higher.",
 (0.046 - 0.040) * 10000000),
("A swap designated as a cash flow hedge rises in fair value from zero to $150,000 during the year. The entry records a debit to the swap asset and a credit to:",
 "OCI of $150,000", ["Earnings of $150,000", "Debt of $150,000", "Interest expense of $150,000"],
 "In a cash flow hedge the derivative's $150,000 gain goes to other comprehensive income until the hedged interest payments affect earnings.",
 150000),
("A company buys a foreign currency forward to hedge the price of inventory it expects to buy from a foreign supplier next quarter. The hedge is a:",
 "Cash flow hedge", ["Fair value hedge", "Net investment hedge", "Trading position"],
 "A hedge of a forecasted transaction, here a future inventory purchase, protects against variability in cash flows. A firm commitment could instead be hedged as a fair value hedge."),
("In a fair value hedge of fixed-rate debt, the swap's fair value falls by $90,000 and the debt's fair value for the hedged risk also falls by $90,000. The net effect on earnings is:",
 "No net effect", ["A $90,000 loss", "A $90,000 gain", "A $180,000 loss"],
 "The $90,000 loss on the swap and the $90,000 gain from reducing the debt's carrying amount both go to earnings and offset."),
]
